WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.220
A 2 million light-year radio structure shaped like a treble clef was re-energized by a galaxy cluster collision. This is Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 227. Chandra X-ray observatory data from the National Aeronautics and Space Administration, or NASA, together with E. Rosita, show the charged particles were first launched by a supermassive black hole. The original radio emission from that cloud then faded. A composite image presents the radio emission in red and newly detected X-rays in blue.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:34.260
The feature stays invisible in optical light because the disc of the Milky Way sits in front

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:34.600
of it.

00:00:35.318 --> 00:00:41.058
The object was first examined in 2004, and its origin stayed unclear until the new X-ray

00:00:41.058 --> 00:00:41.838
data arrived.

00:00:42.478 --> 00:00:48.918
Image processing draws X-rays from the Chandra X-ray Center, INA-5RA, and A-Botion and

00:00:48.918 --> 00:00:54.938
colleagues, infrared from UKIDSS GPS, and radio from Astron low-far.

00:00:54.938 --> 00:01:00.798
That span runs roughly 20 times the diameter of the Milky Way, a signal crossing it left

00:01:00.798 --> 00:01:05.578
its source before our species existed, right along with one of those ancient electrons

00:01:05.578 --> 00:01:07.478
as the merger shock front arrives.

00:01:08.198 --> 00:01:10.218
Magnetic fields suddenly tighten around it.

00:01:10.678 --> 00:01:12.778
The particle's energy jumps under that squeeze.

00:01:13.398 --> 00:01:17.998
What had gone dim becomes a luminous radio source that can be mapped across the space between

00:01:17.998 --> 00:01:18.518
galaxies.

00:01:19.178 --> 00:01:23.838
Magnetic reconnection of the kind that drives flares on the Sun is running here at the scale

00:01:23.838 --> 00:01:29.418
of an entire galaxy cluster. The x-ray signature of the shock sits exactly where the revived

00:01:29.418 --> 00:01:35.278
radio glow appears. That match confirms both the timing and the location of the re-acceleration.

00:01:35.898 --> 00:01:40.838
Energy injected by supermassive black holes can persist in intergalactic space for millions

00:01:40.838 --> 00:01:46.598
of years before a larger dynamical event taps it again. Relic plasma can store that energy

00:01:46.598 --> 00:01:51.918
long after the original outburst fades. The precise efficiency with which a passing shock

00:01:51.918 --> 00:01:54.638
pores energy back into the plasma is still unknown.

00:01:55.418 --> 00:01:57.838
Observers can locate where the particles light up.

00:01:58.358 --> 00:02:02.818
They cannot yet explain why some relic plasma is respond dramatically while other stayed

00:02:02.818 --> 00:02:03.098
dark.

00:02:03.738 --> 00:02:07.078
That gap hides a simple question about the space between galaxies.

00:02:07.718 --> 00:02:11.038
How much energy still sits there unseen in faded plasma?

00:02:11.658 --> 00:02:15.598
How often a cluster merger resets the clock on those ancient radio fossils?

00:02:16.198 --> 00:02:20.998
The exact fraction of relic plasma that lights up during any given merger remains an open

00:02:20.998 --> 00:02:24.038
variable in models of cosmic magnetism.

00:02:24.038 --> 00:02:27.978
Future X-ray and radio surveys may map more of these revived structures.

00:02:28.991 --> 00:02:34.211
Ken Schreiber put up $400,000 so the Ogles County Historical Society could acquire

00:02:34.211 --> 00:02:36.011
Neil Armstrong's Boyhood House.

00:02:36.591 --> 00:02:41.691
Fizz.org identifies Schreiber as a former United States Air Force fighter pilot and an

00:02:41.691 --> 00:02:43.011
American Airlines captain.

00:02:43.611 --> 00:02:48.551
The two-story home stands at 601 West Benton Street in Wapakoneta, Ohio.

00:02:48.551 --> 00:02:53.031
The young Neil built model planes there and tested them in a basement wind tunnel.

00:02:53.531 --> 00:02:57.851
The house has not been open to the public, even with museum goers stopping by often.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:04.651
The society plans to restore the 1940s interior and open the home for tours by 2030, the

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.171
centennial of Armstrong's birth.

00:03:06.751 --> 00:03:11.071
The sale is scheduled to be finalized soon, after which restoration research will begin

00:03:11.071 --> 00:03:11.551
in earnest.

00:03:12.271 --> 00:03:16.691
Previous owner Karen Mikesell hosted nine astronauts, including Buzz Aldrin.

00:03:17.271 --> 00:03:22.471
Aldrin's visit left him in tears. Armstrong's old bedroom is now decorated with photos and

00:03:22.471 --> 00:03:26.911
paintings of the moon landing, plus autographed photos of astronauts who have been through

00:03:26.911 --> 00:03:31.871
the house. Shriver grew up about 60 miles away and had never toured the house until this

00:03:31.871 --> 00:03:37.311
summer. During that visit, he recalled imagining Armstrong running up and down the stairs. He

00:03:37.311 --> 00:03:44.971
surprised even himself by stepping forward after reading that the property was for sale, and

00:03:44.971 --> 00:03:49.311
drew on his own years as a military pilot to recognize what the modest Ohio residents

00:03:49.311 --> 00:03:49.711
meant.

00:03:50.231 --> 00:03:53.831
The home went up for sale in August for the first time in nearly 40 years.

00:03:54.391 --> 00:03:57.351
The same family had owned it since the mid-1960s.

00:03:57.871 --> 00:04:02.371
Mike Sell, who is 82, had hoped someone would buy the house to help preserve it and inspire

00:04:02.371 --> 00:04:03.351
future generations.

00:04:03.991 --> 00:04:08.991
The Ogles County Historical Society will now own the home outright and can restore it without

00:04:08.991 --> 00:04:10.811
the uncertainty of private ownership.

00:04:10.811 --> 00:04:16.630
Historians have already started archival work on what the house would have looked like in the 1940s.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:21.130
They are talking with community leaders about raising money to renovate and maintain it.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:25.590
The layout where young Neil conducted experiments and built models is still there.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:32.360
Astronomers report a magnetic eruption near a supermassive black hole that exhibits the new purd effect.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:37.560
A paper submitted to the astrophysical journal letters, shared via space subreddit,

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:40.840
presents the detection as the first of its kind at that scale.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:45.300
The new purd effect has been measured in solar flares since 1968.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.260
The event is a magnetic reconnection outburst.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:53.120
The finding indicates the same underlying physics functions across enormous differences

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:53.640
in scale.

00:04:54.718 --> 00:04:59.238
The Ogles County Historical Society is due to close on the Wapa Kaneta House shortly,

00:04:59.698 --> 00:05:04.538
and the first hard look at restoring that 1940s interior begins once the sale is done.

00:05:05.258 --> 00:05:10.238
After that closing, it will be clearer what the 2030 public opening still needs in funding

00:05:10.238 --> 00:05:15.718
and archival work. That's fascinating frontiers for today. If you enjoyed this, a rating

